{
    "background_story": "Abdiel was a jovial music teacher who spent most of his free time spreading holiday cheer as a caroler. Every winter, he would gather a group of friends and students to form a festive choir, singing classic carols in harmony. Abdiel's rich baritone voice and infectious enthusiasm made him a natural leader, and his group quickly became a beloved fixture in the community. For years, they would visit nursing homes, hospitals, and town squares, sharing the joy of music with those who needed it most. Abdiel's love of caroling was more than just a hobby - it was a way to bring people together and remind them of the true spirit of the season. His group's performances were always met with applause and smiles, and Abdiel's heart swelled with pride knowing he was making a difference, one carol at a time.",
